<title>INDIA: Indian parliament approves 1996/97 general budget.</title>
<headline>Indian parliament approves 1996/97 general budget.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's upper house, Rajya Sabha approved on Friday, the finance bill for 1996/97 (April-March) giving effect to the budget proposals for the year, officials said.</p>
<p>It completed parliamentary endorsement of the general budget that Finance Minister P. Chidambaram presented in July. The lower house, Lok Sabha, had approved it on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bill takes effect after an assent from the president, which is considered a formality.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom, +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
